course: dictionary
lesson: 9990
title: Teddy and its friends
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Teddy is a noun, so it names a thing. A teddy is a soft toy bear made of furry cloth and stuffed so it is cuddly. «I still sleep with my old teddy» tells you the teddy is a toy the speaker holds close at bedtime. Teddy bear means the same thing.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so check the clues. A teddy can also be any favourite soft cuddly toy, not only a bear. Look at «Dad and his partner have a baby, and Teddy sees Dad cuddling her and feels replaced.» Here Teddy starts with a capital letter, so it is a name for a person, not a toy.
explain: Good readers ask: what does the word do in this sentence? Is it a thing, a person or a feeling? Then swap in your meaning and check it still makes sense. «The koala looks like a teddy bear that sleeps all day» uses teddy to describe how the koala looks, and the clue sleeps all day tells you that it is cuddly and sleepy.
fact: A teddy is a soft toy bear made of furry cloth and stuffed so it is cuddly.
fact: A teddy can also be any favourite soft cuddly toy.
fact: Schools hold «teddy bears' picnics», where children bring their favourite toys.
fact: It is said the teddy bear was named after US President Theodore «Teddy» Roosevelt, who refused to shoot a tied-up bear.
fact: «The koala looks like a teddy bear that sleeps all day» is a comparison; the koala really does rest for up to about 20 hours.
exercise: «I still sleep with my old teddy.» What is a teddy in this sentence? | A small, sharp tool | A hard plastic robot | A type of cake | *A soft toy the speaker cuddles
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Telling everyone a friend's secret got the whole class teasing him.» that means making fun of someone. | friend | *teasing | class | secret
exercise: «The koala looks like a teddy bear that sleeps all day.» What does the comparison suggest? | The koala can talk to people | The koala is made of cloth and stuffed | The koala is very fast and loud | *The koala looks cuddly and sleepy, like a teddy
test: What is the plural of teddy? | teddyes | *teddies | teddys | teddie
test: «Dad and his partner have a baby, and Teddy sees Dad cuddling her and feels replaced.» Why might Teddy feel replaced? | Dad gave him a new toy | *He feels his place with Dad has been taken by the baby | He wants to go to a teddy bears' picnic | Dad is going away on a trip
exam: Which of these is a teddy, using the meaning of any favourite soft cuddly toy? | *A soft rabbit that a child cuddles every night | A wooden spoon | A glass of milk | A plastic robot
